Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline updates a chronic-pain-management-recommendation on a new-evidence-basis.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline should assist a clinician in an opioid-pain-medication-benefit-and-risk-weighing for a painful-acute-condition.
Every opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline should assist a clinician in an opioid-pain-medication-benefit-and-risk-weighing for a procedure-related-pain.
A painful-acute-condition-example includes a low-back-pain-example and includes a neck-pain-example and includes an other-musculoskeletal-pain-example and includes a neuropathic-pain-example and includes a dental-pain-example and includes a kidney-stone-pain-example and includes an acute-episodic-migraine-example.
A procedure-related-pain-example includes a postoperative-pain-example and includes an oral-surgery-pain-example.
